Cell["\<\
Definition: a line is an inextensible geodesic \[LongDash] a shortest path \
that no neighbour of either end prolongs.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"bf2c21e8-0861-47ed-ae6e-8d0cd93a60f6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Its graph \[LongDash] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraMeasurement"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMeasurement", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["line", "TI"], ",", " ", "\"\<Graph\>\""}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cb9ff7ed-351d-4a0a-a728-2f6383978163"],
 " \[LongDash] is a ",
 Cell[BoxData["List"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0775c6ed-453f-44dc-9c4a-727cbe44040f"],
 " of DAGs, one per pair of ends (",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 ") that is compatible, ",
 StyleBox["d(a, b) = d(a, p) + d(p, q) + d(q, b)", "TI"],
 ", and maximal, no neighbour of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " or ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " lengthening ",
 StyleBox["d(a, b)", "TI"],
 ". The DAG for (",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 ") is the union of the intervals ",
 StyleBox["I(a, p)", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["I(p, q)", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["I(q, b)", "TI"],
 ". Its chains are exactly the lines with those ends, and every line is a \
chain of exactly one DAG, so ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Faithful\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c81ac449-495a-40b5-86d1-0832537a71d9"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData["True"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0e00e158-fa8d-426d-81c1-db05051eeede"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f87c5d40-dcf8-433b-a720-bc8e575f2495"],

Cell["\<\
The list is not optional. The union of the DAGs can carry chains that are not \
geodesics: through the edge 1\[Dash]2 of the 6-cycle there are three DAGs and \
three lines, while their union would add a fourth path that is not a geodesic.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"bebcb5e1-a6e7-4aad-90a1-bede1c047f62"],

Cell["\<\
The DAGs are alternatives, so the counts add across them. The family can be \
astronomical while the list stays small.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"38b539b2-2af4-422e-a231-0c00f96a85a4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " = ",
 StyleBox["q", "TI"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraLine"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraLine", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "140a9520-b049-49ff-b4e0-fc905a322272"],
 " is every maximal geodesic through ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 ", once per orientation."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"40d97084-180d-486d-b240-bad09561ed60"]
}, Open  ]],

